<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>1.8.4: Writing Equations Given Dimensions of Shapes</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00193</md:content-id>
    <md:title>1.8.4: Writing Equations Given Dimensions of Shapes</md:title>
    <md:uuid>6b3cc789-b740-4129-80d5-ea00371282b4</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Cool Down Activity</title>
<para>The perimeter of a rectangle is 48 centimeters. The relationship between the length, the width, and the perimeter of the rectangle can be described with the equation: \( 2 \cdot \text{length} +2 \cdot \text{width}=48 \).</para>
<para>Find the length, in centimeters, if the width is:</para>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="835e08ba-dafa-49e1-ba20-cadb1dad296d" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="0" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--Q1-->
  <exercise data-content-id="7ffc205b-b5c3-4b88-9038-cd798a83705e" data-problem-comparator="float" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="14">
    <problem>
      <para>10 centimeters
        </para>
      <para>Enter your answer here.</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 14</para>
      <para>\(2L + 2(10) = 48\)</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q2-->
  <exercise data-content-id="07c3d8c2-ec3b-4992-90ee-3e264fc0822f" data-problem-comparator="float" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="2">
    <problem>
      <para>3.6 centimeters
        </para>
      <para>Enter your answer here.</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 2</para>
      <para>\(2L + 2(3.6) = 48\)</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Do not edit below line.-->
  <solution>
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
